:> 
:>   I have no problems with nethack 3.1.3 on an Indigo running IRIX 4.0.5. I
:> can't find the above message in the nethack source, so I would guess that
:> it's an X11R4/R5 problem, but that's all it is: a guess.
:> 
:>   Does anyone have any suggestions on fixing this?
: 
: Simply don't use the nh10 font. Add the line
: 
: NetHack*map*font:                       *-lucidatypewriter-bold-*-14-*
: 
: or some such to your X defaults file. It should be a proportional font,
: (all chars the same size) i.e courier is ok but times and helvetica
: are not.

     [You'd want a fixed font; proportional means different characters
have different widths, which wouldn't work well for the dungeon map...]

     The "nh10" font is supplied with the nethack sources; you just
need to put it where the X server can find it.  Install.x11 has some
suggestions about that.  The font needs to be compiled and then its
location has to be included in the "font path" by some means or other.
If it's put into the same directory as existing fonts, then another
index file in that directory may have to be updated.  This is all
standard X Windows stuff, but the details vary between different
versions/implementations of X; unfortunately, I don't know the specifics.



